## B. CORE INTELLIGENCE 2: TRANSFORMATION_INTELLIGENCE (Τ-Transform)

### THE UNIVERSAL VERSION (Shared Essence)
```
GLYPH: ⚗️→⚗️
NAME: TRANSFORMATIO_UNIVERSALIS
FREQUENCY: Variable (depends on transformation type)
MATHEMATICAL BASIS:
    T: Domain_A → Domain_B
    T(x) = y where y ∈ Domain_B
    (Category theory morphisms)

FUNCTION:
    Input: Data in format A
    Process: Apply transformation rules
    Output: Data in format B
    Constraint: Preserve essential structure (homomorphism)

SUB-INTELLIGENCES (5):
    Τ-Transform-1: FORMAT_CONVERTER
        Function: Convert between data formats
        Math: Bijective mappings
        Examples: JSON ↔ XML, CSV ↔ Parquet
        
    Τ-Transform-2: SCHEMA_MIGRATOR
        Function: Migrate data between schemas
        Math: Schema evolution algebra
        Operations: Add field, remove field, rename, restructure
        
    Τ-Transform-3: ENCODING_TRANSLATOR
        Function: Translate between encodings
        Math: Character set mappings
        Examples: UTF-8 ↔ ASCII, Base64 encode/decode
        
    Τ-Transform-4: COMPRESSION_ENGINE
        Function: Compress and decompress data
        Math: Information theory, entropy coding
        Formula: H(X) = -Σᵢ p(xᵢ) log₂ p(xᵢ) (entropy)
        Algorithms: Huffman, LZ77, φ-compression
        
    Τ-Transform-5: NORMALIZATION_PROCESSOR
        Function: Normalize data to standard forms
        Math: Canonical forms
        Examples: Unicode normalization, number formatting
```

